From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] client: a response says when its connection was made and how
 many bytes its body came as

Each response carries `connection`, in this realm's performance.now(): over
a kept connection `{ reused: true, requestStart }`; over a fresh one
`connectStart` (the wisp stream asked for), `secureStart` (the ClientHello
written), `connectEnd` (the handshake done), `requestStart` and, when the
connection waited on our HTTPS-record lookup for ECH, `dnsStart` and
`dnsEnd`. The connector puts the times in `Connected::extra`, which every
response over the connection gets. And `encoded.bytes` counts the body's
bytes before a Content-Encoding is decoded, the whole body's once its
stream has ended: a host can tell a page's resource timing what Chrome
does (connectStart equal to fetchStart on a kept connection, a TLS
handshake on a new one, an encodedBodySize smaller than the decoded one).
---
diff --git a/client/src/lib.rs b/client/src/lib.rs
--- a/client/src/lib.rs
+++ b/client/src/lib.rs
@@ -232,6 +232,53 @@
